### api/notifications -- the caller's own notifications (M5 PR a)
#
# Needs an Auth0 access token (see me.http). Put a notification id in .env as
# `notificationId=…` (from the list below).

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv baseUrl}}
@accessToken = {{$dotenv accessToken}}
@notificationId = {{$dotenv notificationId}}

###
# @name listMyNotifications
# 200 { items, nextCursor }, newest first. Render the text from `type` + `params` in the
# reader's language; `link` is computed now (null when the project is gone or not
# readable by the caller), `invite.status` says whether Accept/Reject still applies.
# Pass nextCursor back as cursor; a bad cursor or a limit over the maximum is 400.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me/notifications?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name unreadCount
# 200 { count }. Cheap: the frontend polls it about once a minute.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name markNotificationRead
# 204. Idempotent. Someone else's notification id is 404, the same body as an unknown id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/me/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name markAllNotificationsRead
# 200 { updated }: how many were unread.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/me/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
